course: dictionary
lesson: 2637
title: The word destruction
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Destruction is a noun. It means destroying something so badly that it is ruined or no longer exists. In «War means killing and destruction», the word tells you that war wrecks things as well as hurting people.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. In «Pride goes before destruction, a haughty spirit before a fall», the destruction comes after the pride, so it is the ruin that follows. Ask yourself: what was broken or lost? Then check your meaning by putting it into the sentence.
explain: Destruction can describe the damage left after a storm, fire, war or accident, as in «a path of destruction». It can also be used in a more formal way for the ruin of someone's hopes, health or life. Usually it has no plural, so you write destruction, not destructions.
fact: Destruction means destroying something so badly that it is ruined or no longer exists.
fact: Destruction can also mean the damage left after a storm, fire, war or accident.
fact: «A path of destruction» means a route along which everything was badly damaged.
fact: «Mass destruction» means destruction on a very large scale.
fact: Destruction is usually a noun with no plural, so write «destruction», not «destructions».
exercise: «War means killing and destruction, and the people who start or run wars often do not want to say that plainly.» What does destruction mean here? | *Things badly broken and ruined | Quiet, peaceful days | Long walks in the hills | A good party
exercise: Proverbs 16:18 says «Pride goes before destruction, a haughty spirit before a fall». What comes before the destruction, according to the verse? | Rain | *Pride | Sleep | Music
exercise: «The tornado left a path of destruction across the village.» What does the phrase suggest? | A new road built for cars | A quiet walk by the river | A happy festival with music | *Terrible damage, with things wrecked along the way
test: «The volcano caused destruction for miles around.» What does destruction mean? | A new farm | A lovely view of the mountain | A wet day with grey clouds | *Great damage, with everything ruined
test: Which word is closest in meaning to destruction? | Breakfast | Gift | *Ruin | Lullaby
exam: Which sentence uses destruction correctly? | Destruction is a fast little animal that ran away. | The flood was destructions of the town, big and wet. | The flood caused great destruction to the town. | *The flood caused great destruction to the town, wrecking homes and roads.
